.KEY x
.BRA {
.KET }
;
; xSysInfo's own report, as one more data point (sdcard.md sec.11).
;
; FULL writes to the CLI instead of opening the GUI -- src/main.c's template is
; "DEBUG/S,BRIEF/S,FULL/S,DARK/S" -- which is the only reason this can be run
; from a script at all.
;
; Written to the card, not to DEBUG:. An Echo or a redirect to DEBUG: from a
; boot script produces nothing on the serial line here -- verified across two
; separate runs of two different boot tests -- so a probe that reports that way
; reports nothing at all. SDCARD0P0: is where S:Startup-Sequence already sends
; the AddUSBHardware log for the same reason, and the file can be read out of
; the image afterwards with mtype.
;
Echo >"SDCARD0P0:sysinfo.log" "[sysinfo] xSysInfo FULL"
xSysInfo FULL >>"SDCARD0P0:sysinfo.log"
Echo >>"SDCARD0P0:sysinfo.log" "[sysinfo] done"
